    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40254" root="نفس" body-key="n">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انفس</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَفُسَ</span>, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انفسهُ</span> <i>It</i>
(a thing, TA) <i>pleased him,</i> (K, TA,) <i>and made
him desirous of it:</i> (TA:) or <i>became highly
esteemed by him.</i> (IKtt.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْفَسَنى فِيهِ</span> <i>He
made me desirous of it;</i> (S, M, A, K:) as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَّسَنِى فيه</span>, (IAar, M, TA,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِهِ</span>. (So in my
copy of the A.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَنْفَسَهُ</span> <i>How powerful is his
evil,</i> or <i>envious, eye!</i> (Lh, M.)

